I'm sure you're aware of the names of the at least the majority of the
letterals in Lojban ( {.abu}, {by.}, etc.). The names of "." and "," in
Lojban are, respectively, {denpa bu} and {slaka bu}.

The Dot Side doesn't refer to using letterals as pro-sumti, as in the {by.}
in {la.benjis. gerku .i by. barda}. It refers to the practice of leading
cmevla with a "." so that the latterals groups "la", "lai", and "doi" can
be used in them. (As for example {la.doitcland.} or {la.las,andjeles.}).


